 a lot of sense for all this to be  done only to turn around and make  changes that will take them a few steps  back especially now that they are past  their intended launch date with all that  data put together we may be looking at  fully automated Vehicles soon think of  what you will do with all that free time  when you no longer have to draw Drive  having said that we know Tesla is not  one to blend in with the crowd and the  manufacturers always go the extra mile  to ensure the vehicles are an instant  hit among the eager fan base one aspect  where the Cyber truck stands out from  other automated electric vehicles on the  market is its exceptional features such  as the integration of an internet  connection within the truck no matter  where you drive it yep that's right you  can take it into the Wilderness without  worrying about losing connection with  the rest of the world doesn't that sound  futuristic let's see what the hype is  about internet connection inside the  truck the new cybertruck prototype  features a limited starlink internet  connection as soon as SpaceX deploys  their second generation of communication  satellites that doesn't sound like a  whole lot of internet at first but it's  not a bad deal when you consider that  this service is mostly reserved for use  in the wilderness it is highly unlikely  that there will be crowds trying to use  the limited connection compounding the  problem so although you can't Vlog or  even stream your favorite shows this  connection is enough to send out a text  message message and to have a voice call  which is all you need to alert people of  emergency situations and maybe the  difference between life and death the  internet connection update was announced  after SpaceX and T-Mobile's partnership  announcement which will see updated  starlink satellites connecting directly  with mobile phones so the internet  connection by starlink will be from a  portion of Tesla's already existing 5G  Network spectrum that 